{"audio":"voice-tight.wav","hash":"b5560777db3aa209","durationSec":333.893,"text":"If you had bought last year's stock every single January since 2000, your \u00a31 ,000 would have been worth about \u00a330 by 2011. The same 1 ,000 in the S &P 500, left completely alone, is about 9 ,000 today. It never once dropped below 750. So I ran the whole race, year by year. I'll show you every year's winner and what it did next. The one year where the hype paid off spectacularly, and at the end, the number from the biggest study ever done on this. It settles the argument. First, the rules, because the rules are the whole point. Pot one is the boring pot. $1 ,000 into an S &P 500 index fund in January 2000. The dividends reinvested, never touched again. Pot two is the hype pot. Every January buys the stock that was the best performer in the S &P 500 year before. The one in every headline and holds it for 12 months, then it sells it and buys a new winner. Now the race, and the first 12 years are brutal. In 2000, the hottest stock was an energy trader called DINAGY, up more than 200 % behind it. The hype pot bought that in January 2001, and it fell 54%. In 2001, the winner was in video, up 308%. The hype pot bought that, and in 2002, it lost 83%. Two years in, the 1 ,085 pounds. Sit with that one. In video, the company everyone is chasing today was the best stock in the index in 2001. Buy in the January after and you lose 83%. Being right about the company is not the same as being right about the price. Then a few decent years. Avaya, Autodesk, Valero, Allegheny Technologies, up a bit. Then flat. Then 2007's winner, National Oilwell Varko, bought in 2008 of January, lost 67 % in the crash. Then Netflix, the best stock of 2010, lost 61 % in 2011. By the end of 2011, the hype pots, 1 ,000 is 30%. Down 97%. 12 years of buying the stock everyone was talking about. The boring pot, about 1 ,280. It had been through the dot com crash and the 2008 crash, and it was still standing. Not exciting. Standing. Then the story turns, and this is the part the hype merchants will quote at you. From 2017, the hype pot gets lucky. In video, the best stock of 2016 goes up another 81%. AMD wins 2 years running and the hype pot rides it and goes up 140%. Then 100%. Tesla, Devon Energy, then in video again, up 171 % in 2024. Then Palantir, up 135 % last year. 9 years of being right, almost in a row. Here is the hype pot at the end of 2025. After sitting at 30 pounds in 2011, about 7 ,200. The boring pot, about 9 ,000. 9 straight years of picking the winners follow up, and it still is not caught up. And look at what you have to sit through to get there. This is in videos charts since 2018. The hype pot earned this stock in 2002, when it felt 83%. And it sold it at the bottom, because the rules said buy the new winner. The hype pot never earned it on the way up to 2017. And this year, last year's winner was Sandisk, and it is nearly 400 % so far. So right now, in October 2026, the hype pot is ahead for the first time in 26 years. That is the trap. It always looks like it's about to work. But to be here, you had to watch 1 ,000 become 30 pounds. Hold a stock that lost 83%. Sell it and never once flinched for a decade. Nobody does that. And this is what the boring pot looks like from the inside. An S &P 500 index fund bought in 2020 and left alone, up about 130 % since the start. Nothing clever ever happened here. Nobody touched it. And the number I promised you at the start. A professor called Hendrick Besson buying the study of every US stock since 1926. 26 ,000 companies. 4 % of them about in 2019 made all of the market gains. The other 96 put together did no better than cash. Most individual stocks lose money over their life. You cannot guess which 4%. Nobody can. But an index fund owns all of them automatically. And it bought Nvidia in 2001 and never sold. So here's the boring way. One index fund, global S &P 500. The same amount every month. Inside an ISO so the growth rate is tax -free. Dividends reinvested. Nothing sold. None of this is financial advice. And the past is not a promise in the future. It's just 26 years of maths and the maths does not care about how exciting the stock is. The high pot. A decade at 30 pounds for 7 ,200 today. The boring pot. 9 ,000 and you never lost sleep. 4 % of companies make all of the gains and the index fund owns every single one of them. Monthly in an ISO. Hands off. Tell me in the comments, honestly. Which stock would you have chased in 2000?","words":[{"w":"If","s":0.53,"e":1.35},{"w":"you","s":1.35,"e":1.47},{"w":"had","s":1.47,"e":1.59},{"w":"bought","s":1.59,"e":1.77},{"w":"last","s":1.77,"e":2.03},{"w":"year's","s":2.03,"e":2.33},{"w":"stock","s":2.33,"e":2.49},{"w":"every","s":2.49,"e":2.85},{"w":"single","s":2.85,"e":3.37},{"w":"January","s":3.37,"e":3.61},{"w":"since","s":3.61,"e":3.95},{"w":"2000,","s":3.95,"e":4.55},{"w":"your","s":5.01,"e":5.11},{"w":"\u00a31","s":5.11,"e":5.29},{"w":",000","s":5.29,"e":5.59},{"w":"would","s":5.59,"e":6.09},{"w":"have","s":6.09,"e":6.23},{"w":"been","s":6.23,"e":6.41},{"w":"worth","s":6.41,"e":6.71},{"w":"about","s":6.71,"e":6.93},{"w":"\u00a330","s":6.93,"e":7.41},{"w":"by","s":7.41,"e":7.85},{"w":"2011.","s":7.85,"e":8.31},{"w":"The","s":9.15,"e":9.59},{"w":"same","s":9.59,"e":9.81},{"w":"1","s":9.81,"e":10.03},{"w":",000","s":10.03,"e":10.39},{"w":"in","s":10.39,"e":10.51},{"w":"the","s":10.51,"e":10.59},{"w":"S","s":10.59,"e":10.67},{"w":"&P","s":10.67,"e":10.89},{"w":"500,","s":10.89,"e":11.11},{"w":"left","s":11.47,"e":11.53},{"w":"completely","s":11.53,"e":11.87},{"w":"alone,","s":11.87,"e":12.21},{"w":"is","s":12.21,"e":12.43},{"w":"about","s":12.43,"e":12.59},{"w":"9","s":12.59,"e":12.91},{"w":",000","s":12.91,"e":13.25},{"w":"today.","s":13.25,"e":13.49},{"w":"It","s":14.25,"e":14.41},{"w":"never","s":14.41,"e":14.69},{"w":"once","s":14.69,"e":15.03},{"w":"dropped","s":15.03,"e":15.19},{"w":"below","s":15.19,"e":15.49},{"w":"750